   "html_text": "From 1958 through 1967, Feyerabend developed his normative approach to epistemology in a series of papers on problems of empiricism that attempted to contribute to a positive model for the acquisition of knowledge. In these papers, he unpacks the consequences of his views on meaning and method, while criticizing his contemporaries’ accounts. These strange ideas emerged from his earlier engagement with the Vienna Circle’s protocol sentence debate and appear in their initial form in his 1951 Ph.D.",
   "md_text": "From 1958 through 1967, Feyerabend developed his normative approach to epistemology in a series of papers on problems of empiricism that attempted to contribute to a positive model for the acquisition of knowledge. In these papers, he unpacks the consequences of his views on meaning and method, while criticizing his contemporaries’ accounts. These strange ideas emerged from his earlier engagement with the Vienna Circle’s protocol sentence debate and appear in their initial form in his 1951 Ph.D."
